source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-22
observed: Brackets around the URL make it a link rather than an autolink, and Jira drops them, so jiro warns.
-- input.jira --
{{[http://example.com] x}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt><a href="http://example.com" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">http://example.com</a> x</tt></p>
-- want.md --
`[http://example.com] x`
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "inline-code",
  "Reason": "Jira would render a link inside this Monospace Span; inline code keeps the characters literal"
 }
]
